WEBVTT

00:51.200 --> 00:54.035
Thanks for encouraging us
to come to Gay Pride Day, Brian.

00:54.070 --> 00:55.431
Yeah, this seems
like it'll be fun.

00:55.454 --> 00:57.539
Real fun, not "entertain-
your-wife's-parents-

00:57.590 --> 00:59.507
while-your-wife-
is-at-work" fun.

00:59.542 --> 01:02.378
Laura gets home at 7:00,
so I figure we can stare

01:02.412 --> 01:04.280
at our wine glasses
till then.

01:08.552 --> 01:10.286
So, uh... so, when...

01:10.320 --> 01:13.089
when do you guys think
you're gonna die?

01:15.792 --> 01:17.343
Wow, a parade.

01:17.362 --> 01:18.729
It's like I'm walking
past stuff,

01:18.780 --> 01:20.330
but I'm not going anywhere.

01:20.365 --> 01:23.517
Look, there's the float
commemorating sham marriages.

01:23.551 --> 01:25.986
Sorry, this stomach thing
is acting up again tonight.

01:26.020 --> 01:29.289
Oh, and I'm going on a business
trip to Mykonos for July.

01:29.356 --> 01:33.126
And it says this next one is
the "Shocking Reveal Gay Float."

01:33.162 --> 01:35.163
(gasps)

01:36.215 --> 01:39.067
I had no idea.

01:39.069 --> 01:40.334
Hey, check it out.

01:40.369 --> 01:41.969
There's an air show.

01:45.107 --> 01:46.641
Oh, my God--
they're gonna crash!

01:46.675 --> 01:48.409
No, no, don't worry--
it's a gay air show.

01:48.444 --> 01:50.129
They're just gonna
lightly touch tips.

01:51.314 --> 01:53.365
CROWD:
Aw!

01:53.400 --> 01:55.234
Well, listen up, everybody,
'cause it's time

01:55.268 --> 01:57.236
for our grand prize drawing
for those tickets

01:57.270 --> 02:00.038
to see Celine Dion live
in Las Vegas!

02:00.073 --> 02:01.807
DEEP VOICE (over speaker):
Infertility!

02:01.841 --> 02:03.008
Here we go!

02:03.042 --> 02:04.843
Our grand prize winner is...

02:04.878 --> 02:06.713
Brian Griffin.

02:07.832 --> 02:09.582
(all clamoring)

02:09.617 --> 02:10.834
Wow, I don't believe it!

02:10.868 --> 02:12.152
Hey, congratulations, buddy.

02:12.186 --> 02:13.386
You know, you're a lucky guy.

02:13.421 --> 02:16.122
The only thing I ever won
was an extra day of summer.

02:17.091 --> 02:19.259
Okay, Peter--
one more day.

02:19.293 --> 02:21.277
Yay!

02:22.412 --> 02:24.482
I saw what I look like
in a car window,

02:24.516 --> 02:26.183
and now I don't want to go.

02:29.688 --> 02:31.555
<i>ANNOUNCER: We now return
to Franklin and Bash</i>

02:31.590 --> 02:33.557
<i>with Indicators to Show
Which One is Franklin</i>

02:33.592 --> 02:35.126
<i>and Which One is Bash.</i>

02:35.160 --> 02:38.062
Defensive blows to their heads
were to send a message...

02:38.096 --> 02:39.113
<i>MAN:
Oh, sorry, sorry.</i>

02:39.147 --> 02:41.633
"Help me get
into used car sales."

02:41.667 --> 02:43.601
Hey, Stewie, I don't know if
you have any interest in this,

02:43.619 --> 02:45.504
but I was wondering if you
want to go to Vegas with me

02:45.538 --> 02:46.671
and see Celine Dion.

02:46.706 --> 02:48.573
Are you kidding?
Of course I want to go!

02:48.608 --> 02:50.142
Wow, these are good seats!

02:50.176 --> 02:52.861
I know-- apparently they were
donated by Goldman's Pharmacy.

02:52.895 --> 02:55.197
Turns out Mort's cousin
is Celine's opening act.

02:55.231 --> 02:56.665
Really? What's his talent?

02:56.699 --> 02:58.885
I understand he's a
magician of sorts.

02:58.919 --> 03:00.159
All right, for this next trick,

03:00.187 --> 03:03.005
I need a quarter
from the audience.

03:03.040 --> 03:05.141
Okay, thank you.

03:05.175 --> 03:06.425
(rapid footsteps departing)

03:06.460 --> 03:07.593
(door opens, closes)

03:07.628 --> 03:08.594
(car engine revs)

03:08.629 --> 03:11.130
(tires screech)

03:14.469 --> 03:15.719
You almost ready, Stewie?

03:15.753 --> 03:17.221
We should probably start
heading to the airport.

03:17.255 --> 03:18.989
Yes, I was gonna talk to
you about that, actually.

03:19.023 --> 03:20.557
Last night, I was
thinking to myself,

03:20.592 --> 03:22.759
"Why fly, when we can
get there instantly?"

03:22.794 --> 03:24.027
What? What do you mean?

03:24.062 --> 03:26.029
Well, you see, I recently
completed construction

03:26.064 --> 03:28.382
on a teleportation device,
and it occurred to me,

03:28.416 --> 03:30.702
this may be the perfect
chance to try it out.

03:34.390 --> 03:37.225
Wow, Stewie,
that's incredible!

03:37.259 --> 03:38.927
Oh, hey, guys.

03:38.961 --> 03:41.396
Peter, what do
you have there?

03:41.430 --> 03:44.415
Give me the scissors.

03:44.450 --> 03:46.518
I was just gonna make
some masks!

03:46.552 --> 03:47.720
<i>Use your scissors.</i>

03:47.754 --> 03:49.171
They're not sharp!

03:49.206 --> 03:50.523
(whines)

03:50.557 --> 03:51.757
So, what do you say?

03:51.791 --> 03:53.626
Hmm, teleport to Vegas, huh?

03:53.660 --> 03:55.677
All right, let's do it!

03:57.814 --> 04:00.249
Okay, now, the device is
powered by kinetic energy,

04:00.283 --> 04:02.218
so you've got to dance
to make it work.

04:02.252 --> 04:03.919
You, uh... really?

04:03.954 --> 04:06.873
Yeah , you've
got to dance.

04:06.908 --> 04:08.158
(laughs)

04:08.192 --> 04:09.859
What are you doing,
you tool?

04:09.894 --> 04:11.394
Do you know anything
about science?

04:11.429 --> 04:13.830
You just saw
me program it.

04:17.768 --> 04:19.286
What the hell, Stewie?
It didn't work.

04:19.320 --> 04:20.353
Hmm, that's odd.

04:20.388 --> 04:21.689
It appears there
may still be

04:21.723 --> 04:23.190
a few more bugs
to work out.

04:23.225 --> 04:24.892
Well, it was
worth a try.

04:34.653 --> 04:36.787
Oh, my God, Stewie--
it-it worked!

04:36.822 --> 04:37.940
We're in Vegas!

04:37.974 --> 04:39.408
Yeah, all right!

04:39.442 --> 04:40.926
Well, let's hit the
hospital, get checked

04:40.960 --> 04:44.329
for teleportation
cancer and then party!

04:44.364 --> 04:46.865
Well, since the teleportation
machine failed to get us

04:46.899 --> 04:49.001
to Vegas, I suppose we should
just catch our plane.

04:49.035 --> 04:50.836
I'll repair it
when we get back.

04:50.870 --> 04:53.255
BOTH STEWIES: You know, this is going
to be a good trip, Brian.

04:53.289 --> 04:55.775
I really feel like fate
is on our side.

04:55.809 --> 04:57.510
Scissors are jerks.

04:57.544 --> 04:59.145
And I'm a owl.

05:05.916 --> 05:07.266
Oh, wow, look at
that, Stewie.

05:07.267 --> 05:08.250
Perfect timing.

05:08.285 --> 05:09.385
Oh, it's beautiful.

05:09.419 --> 05:11.621
Everything's just
so beautiful here.

05:11.656 --> 05:13.273
(groans)
This is miserable.

05:13.307 --> 05:16.076
Three-hour delay
and a completely full flight.

05:16.110 --> 05:18.211
Don't look at us,
you (bleep) pig.

05:18.246 --> 05:21.081
Take your Juicy sweatpants
and your dirty pillow from home,

05:21.115 --> 05:24.284
and your bucket of Coke, and
get the hell out of my sight.

05:24.318 --> 05:26.052
What was her problem?

05:29.341 --> 05:30.608
You see that, Brian?

05:30.642 --> 05:33.411
That's going to be our
penises later, right?

05:35.948 --> 05:38.249
Stewie, that teleportation
machine is amazing.

05:38.283 --> 05:39.801
It's so great
that we're already here.

05:39.835 --> 05:41.135
Yep, drink it in, Bri.

05:41.170 --> 05:43.805
Time to enjoy all the
Bellagio has to offer.

05:43.839 --> 05:45.057
Classic architecture.

05:45.091 --> 05:46.158
Beautiful art.

05:46.192 --> 05:47.926
Plus, the air is clean
because they suck up

05:47.961 --> 05:50.796
all the cigarette smoke and
dump it in the bad hotels.

05:50.830 --> 05:52.698
Smell that, kids?

05:52.732 --> 05:55.284
It's been in a rich
person's mouth.

05:55.318 --> 05:57.002
Hi. We're checking in--
Griffin?

05:57.036 --> 05:58.270
Ah, yes.

05:58.304 --> 05:59.938
I see you've requested
a bed that's good

05:59.973 --> 06:00.939
for bouncing
and jumping?

06:00.974 --> 06:01.941
That is correct.

06:01.976 --> 06:03.109
I am a businessman.

06:03.143 --> 06:04.477
Just sign here, please.

06:04.512 --> 06:06.546
And you can actually keep
that pen if you'd like.

06:06.580 --> 06:07.981
No way! Really?

06:08.015 --> 06:09.382
Wow, you see that, Brian?

06:09.416 --> 06:10.783
Good luck already.

06:10.818 --> 06:12.858
You know, I know we're
switching to a digital world,

06:12.887 --> 06:15.889
but I-I think this little
guy's still got a place in it.

06:15.923 --> 06:18.141
Hey, we should try one of those
slot machines by the entrance.

06:18.175 --> 06:20.296
You know, they always set
those things to pay out more

06:20.328 --> 06:22.196
so they can lure people
into the casino.

06:22.230 --> 06:23.564
Well, that's a great idea.

06:30.021 --> 06:31.939
Oh, my God--
I don't believe it!

06:31.973 --> 06:32.806
Brian, we won!

06:32.840 --> 06:34.408
We won the jackpot!

06:34.442 --> 06:35.843
Oh, this is unbelievable.

06:35.862 --> 06:38.680
I haven't had this much fun
since I hosted the Oscars.

06:38.714 --> 06:39.948
Good evening.

06:39.982 --> 06:42.217
I just want to say
that I have the utmost respect

06:42.251 --> 06:43.418
for women everywhere.

06:43.452 --> 06:44.786
And also, the Jews.

06:44.820 --> 06:46.154
Good night.

06:54.631 --> 06:56.031
Oh, thank God,
we're finally here.

06:56.049 --> 06:57.967
That plane ride took forever.

06:58.001 --> 07:01.504
<i>Kind of weird they showed
Flight 93 on Flight 93.</i>

07:01.538 --> 07:03.839
Hi. We're checking in--
Griffin?

07:03.874 --> 07:06.375
Hmm, I do have a Griffin
here, but that room

07:06.410 --> 07:08.010
was checked into hours ago.
What?

07:08.045 --> 07:10.247
Yes, and I'm afraid we have
no other rooms available.

07:10.281 --> 07:12.482
I see-- is there
a less heavy person

07:12.517 --> 07:13.784
that could check again for me?

07:13.818 --> 07:15.152
I'm sorry, we're
all booked up

07:15.186 --> 07:16.787
because the Slut
Convention's in town.

07:16.821 --> 07:18.589
Slut Convention?
Yeah.

07:18.623 --> 07:20.490
They were promised a
single millionaire,

07:20.525 --> 07:22.426
but it's really just a
bunch of horny squirrels

07:22.460 --> 07:23.794
in a rich-guy suit.

07:23.828 --> 07:24.795
(squirrels chittering)
So...

07:24.829 --> 07:27.432
you made your money
in business?

07:27.466 --> 07:30.868
Where's your
room, handsome?

07:30.902 --> 07:33.488
(women screaming)

07:33.522 --> 07:35.023
Can I at least have that pen?

07:35.057 --> 07:36.524
No, that's
Bellagio property.

07:36.558 --> 07:37.659
Aw.

07:37.693 --> 07:39.527
Well, this sucks.
Hey, I'm gonna go try one

07:39.561 --> 07:41.081
of those slot machines
by the entrance.

07:41.096 --> 07:42.932
They always set
those things to pay out more

07:42.966 --> 07:44.800
so they can lure people
into the casino.

07:50.223 --> 07:52.908
(grunts)
Damn it, Vegas!

07:52.943 --> 07:55.861
Excuse me, where can I find
some smoking Asians?

07:55.895 --> 07:57.763
Oh, everywhere? Okay.

08:03.270 --> 08:07.407
♪ Luck be a lady tonight

08:10.127 --> 08:13.997
♪ Luck be a lady tonight

08:16.568 --> 08:19.119
♪ Luck if you've ever been

08:19.137 --> 08:22.056
♪ A lady to begin with

08:22.090 --> 08:26.177
♪ Luck be a lady tonight

08:32.384 --> 08:33.602
♪ Luck let

08:33.636 --> 08:38.790
♪ A gentleman see

08:38.825 --> 08:41.259
♪ How nice a dame you can be

08:44.147 --> 08:46.765
(both laughing)

08:50.154 --> 08:52.321
Oh, my God, this
place is a dump.

08:52.356 --> 08:53.823
Well, let's not be
so quick to judge.

08:53.857 --> 08:55.908
It says here there's
a continental breakfast.

08:55.943 --> 08:58.044
Oh, the continent is Africa.

08:58.078 --> 08:59.518
Stewie, this place
is a complete pit.

08:59.546 --> 09:01.314
I mean, doesn't it seem
weird to you that we have

09:01.348 --> 09:03.199
to re-check-in
every 20 minutes?

09:03.233 --> 09:06.970
Also the porn is free, but we
have to watch it in the lobby.

09:11.292 --> 09:13.260
Okay, let's see if we can
turn this trip around.

09:13.294 --> 09:14.661
I'm gonna try some blackjack.

09:14.696 --> 09:15.729
Here, take $40.

09:15.764 --> 09:17.004
I'm gonna go get
some ice cream.

09:17.032 --> 09:18.816
All right, I'll
catch up with you.

09:18.850 --> 09:20.617
Hey there...

09:20.652 --> 09:21.819
Denise.

09:21.853 --> 09:23.822
How you doing today?
I don't know.

09:23.856 --> 09:26.257
I usually have to check
with my boyfriend first.

09:26.292 --> 09:27.258
Oh.

09:27.293 --> 09:29.127
Uh... hit, please.

09:29.762 --> 09:31.796
24? Crap!

09:31.831 --> 09:33.965
Do you know what it's
like to go to the doctor

09:33.999 --> 09:36.000
and see your own foot
in the garbage can?

09:36.035 --> 09:38.369
Okay, you have a good night.

09:38.437 --> 09:40.506
Hey, Stewie, I need
some more money.

09:40.540 --> 09:42.041
I lost it all, Brian!

09:42.075 --> 09:43.042
What?

09:43.076 --> 09:45.077
Well, I was on my way
to get ice cream

09:45.112 --> 09:48.180
and I passed a roulette table,
and I put it all on 16

09:48.215 --> 09:50.382
because of that
Taylor Swift song, "Sixteen."

09:50.417 --> 09:51.751
That song is
called "Fifteen."

09:51.785 --> 09:52.952
It came up 15!

09:52.986 --> 09:54.954
Stewie, that was all
the money I brought.

09:54.988 --> 09:56.957
I knew I should've brought
Peter instead of you.

09:56.991 --> 09:58.592
Oh, come on, you would've
done much worse with him.

09:58.626 --> 10:01.461
He's got a terrible tell.

10:01.496 --> 10:02.929
(gasps)

10:02.964 --> 10:04.948
("Stars and Stripes Forever"
playing)

10:13.625 --> 10:15.326
Any cards, Peter?

10:15.360 --> 10:16.694
No, I'm good.

10:20.582 --> 10:21.716
Oh, this is gonna be great.

10:21.750 --> 10:23.351
I hear she puts on
an amazing show.

10:23.385 --> 10:25.419
She does-- you'll be
amazed that that voice

10:25.437 --> 10:27.138
comes out of that face.

10:30.026 --> 10:31.693
Oh, thank God,
we made it in time.

10:31.728 --> 10:32.861
I didn't realize how far

10:32.896 --> 10:34.630
that awful hotel is
from the Strip.

10:34.664 --> 10:37.199
The woman who cleaned
our room had no ears.

10:37.901 --> 10:39.368
(beeping)

10:39.402 --> 10:41.003
I'm sorry,
these tickets are invalid.

10:41.037 --> 10:42.271
What?

10:42.305 --> 10:43.739
It's showing that they've
already been scanned.

10:43.773 --> 10:44.973
I can't let you in.

10:45.008 --> 10:47.010
Oh, this trip has
been a disaster.

10:47.044 --> 10:49.379
I know. I actually thought
I was gonna win big

10:49.413 --> 10:51.514
and get that plastic surgery
I always wanted.

10:51.549 --> 10:52.882
Oh, my God!

10:52.917 --> 10:54.134
Look at him.

10:54.168 --> 10:57.003
He's so cute.

10:58.472 --> 11:00.757
I'm small,
so this is okay.

11:05.030 --> 11:06.380
(sighs)
You know what, screw it.

11:06.414 --> 11:08.682
I say we just cut our
losses and fly home.

11:08.717 --> 11:11.068
Yeah, I'm not so sure
about that.

11:11.102 --> 11:12.203
What? Why?

11:12.237 --> 11:14.171
Well, I may have...

11:14.206 --> 11:16.073
And-and you are gonna
laugh about this,

11:16.107 --> 11:17.908
if I know your dark
sense of humor,

11:17.943 --> 11:21.213
but I may have gambled away
our plane tickets.

11:21.247 --> 11:23.114
You what? How do
you even do that?

11:23.149 --> 11:29.237
It's Vegas, Brian.
You can gamble anything.

11:29.272 --> 11:30.772
(ball falls)

11:30.806 --> 11:32.440
I'm sorry, it's 31.

11:32.475 --> 11:33.508
Ow!

11:33.543 --> 11:35.026
How's it going here?

11:35.061 --> 11:37.096
Not great.
I know what you mean.

11:37.130 --> 11:39.432
We just took a pounding
at the craps table.

11:39.466 --> 11:41.634
Look, why don't we just
call Lois and the fat man?

11:41.668 --> 11:42.652
Maybe they can help us.

11:42.686 --> 11:43.886
I don't know about that.

11:43.921 --> 11:45.655
You know that
500 bucks we lost?

11:45.689 --> 11:49.058
I sort of took that from
Lois without asking.

11:49.092 --> 11:51.127
If she finds out it's
all gone, she'll kill me.

11:51.161 --> 11:52.261
Oh.

11:54.499 --> 11:56.767
My buddy's got the inside track.

11:56.801 --> 11:58.035
It's a sure thing.

11:58.069 --> 12:00.103
I like how all your teeth
are different shapes.

12:00.138 --> 12:01.488
Why are you
telling us this?

12:01.522 --> 12:02.856
What do you want from us?

12:02.874 --> 12:04.658
Honestly,
I'm trying to sell my condo,

12:04.692 --> 12:06.894
and I need people to come
to the open house

12:06.928 --> 12:08.562
and talk
about how nice it is.

12:08.596 --> 12:11.683
Wow, the price per square foot
is quite competitive

12:11.717 --> 12:13.484
with similar homes in the area.

12:13.519 --> 12:14.819
Yes, I also love it.

12:14.853 --> 12:16.321
I will likely purchase it

12:16.355 --> 12:18.323
unless others
put in a rival bid.

12:18.357 --> 12:19.657
Well, what's stopping you?

12:19.692 --> 12:21.326
You know, you've always been
so noncommittal

12:21.360 --> 12:22.560
in our relationship.

12:22.595 --> 12:24.329
Do know how much
it hurt my feelings

12:24.363 --> 12:26.297
when you paused before
introducing me to your parents?

12:26.332 --> 12:29.101
And it's the same reason you
didn't take that job in Denver.

12:29.135 --> 12:31.003
I'm sorry I didn't mean
to waste your time.

12:31.037 --> 12:33.639
I just remembered my husband
is a total chicken (bleep).

12:33.673 --> 12:36.809
I'm not 100% sure
what we're doing any more.

12:41.848 --> 12:44.417
It's like I say, the best
thing you can see in Vegas

12:44.452 --> 12:46.219
is bar, bar, bar.

12:46.254 --> 12:48.955
Yeah, and he's not talking
about slot machines.

12:48.990 --> 12:50.323
Ooh!

12:50.358 --> 12:52.525
Stewie, I'm still not sure
this is a great idea.

12:52.560 --> 12:54.861
Relax, Brian; we're betting
on one basketball game.

12:54.895 --> 12:56.162
That's it.

12:56.197 --> 12:58.431
Then we'll be out of debt
and on our way home.

12:58.466 --> 12:59.766
I suppose.
I just wish

12:59.800 --> 13:01.902
we didn't have to borrow money
from a loan shark.

13:01.937 --> 13:03.457
I mean, that guy seemed
pretty serious.

13:03.472 --> 13:05.640
Okay, and just a couple
of remaining items.

13:05.674 --> 13:08.376
Please indicate here
if I look like a schmuck to you.

13:08.410 --> 13:10.011
I'm gonna say no.

13:10.045 --> 13:12.647
Great. Then please check here
and initial there.

13:12.681 --> 13:15.349
Uh, next, do you think
this is some kind of game?

13:15.384 --> 13:17.051
Um, no.

13:17.085 --> 13:18.320
Okay, initial, please.

13:18.354 --> 13:20.055
And finally, my date of birth.

13:26.696 --> 13:28.797
ANNOUNCER: And 'll at it for us here
(horn blows)

13:28.831 --> 13:31.099
with Duke losing
by just three points.

13:31.134 --> 13:34.036
We... we lost, Brian.

13:34.070 --> 13:35.772
Oh
crap, we're screwed.

13:36.940 --> 13:39.142
Hey, Stewie, give me
$100 from the backpack.

13:39.176 --> 13:40.777
I want to pay a
Wayne Neon look-alike

13:40.811 --> 13:42.345
to beat up a
Rita Rudner look-alike.

13:42.379 --> 13:43.880
I'll give you $1,000.

13:43.882 --> 13:45.915
Pay him to beat up Rita Rudner.

13:47.584 --> 13:49.018
Stewie, we got to get
the hell out of here

13:49.053 --> 13:50.333
before that loan shark finds us.

13:50.354 --> 13:52.356
Yes, you're right.

13:53.358 --> 13:54.992
I've got a bad feeling, Brian.

13:55.026 --> 13:56.860
I've got a good
feeling, Brian.

13:56.895 --> 13:58.729
I'm gonna get
me that honey.

14:05.975 --> 14:07.346
I say, Brian,
this backpack feels

14:07.347 --> 14:08.982
a bit lighter
than it did before.

14:09.017 --> 14:10.618
Well, I wasn't gonna
tell you till later,

14:10.635 --> 14:12.586
but I actually used
part of my portion

14:12.604 --> 14:14.855
to take care of some
personal business.

14:14.889 --> 14:17.541
All right, fine.

14:33.542 --> 14:34.709
(phone vibrates)

14:42.352 --> 14:43.802
Hey, boss, it's me.

14:43.837 --> 14:46.197
I just spotted those two idiots
who borrowed all that money.

14:46.223 --> 14:47.690
Yeah, well, now they're
strutting around

14:47.724 --> 14:49.175
in flashy suits.

14:49.209 --> 14:51.844
Don't worry; I'll get that
money back no matter what,

14:51.878 --> 14:53.729
and for sure I'm not
gonna stop first

14:53.763 --> 14:55.781
and get some crepes
in the lobby.

14:55.815 --> 14:57.716
Where can I get
some crepes?

15:03.107 --> 15:04.627
Hey, Stewie,
thanks for coming with me.

15:04.642 --> 15:06.226
This really has been
an amazing trip.

15:06.260 --> 15:07.561
Yeah, it's been great.

15:07.595 --> 15:08.979
Um, listen, Brian,

15:09.013 --> 15:11.081
this might be a good
time to tell you, uh,

15:11.115 --> 15:14.217
I invited, um, somebody

15:14.252 --> 15:15.686
to come to the room.

15:15.721 --> 15:16.888
Well, what do you mean?

15:16.922 --> 15:18.923
(pounding on door)
Oh, that must be him now.

15:20.459 --> 15:23.027
Okay, come on, you look nothing
like your picture in the ad.

15:23.061 --> 15:24.445
Shut up and give
me the money!

15:24.479 --> 15:26.080
What? What the hell
are you talking about?

15:26.114 --> 15:27.949
Okay, I'm starting to think
you're not Apollo.

15:27.983 --> 15:30.351
You bastards think you can
just borrow a bunch of money

15:30.385 --> 15:32.688
from a loan shark and then
waste it on tacky suits?

15:32.722 --> 15:34.790
Tacky?
Sir, I'll have you know

15:34.824 --> 15:36.925
I bought this
in the lobby of a casino.

15:36.960 --> 15:38.026
Well, don't shoot.

15:38.061 --> 15:39.595
You must have us confused
with somebody else.

15:39.629 --> 15:41.396
We didn't borrow
any money, I swear.

15:41.431 --> 15:43.649
Sounds like somebody
wants to die.

15:43.683 --> 15:44.950
Aah! No, no!
Stewie,

15:44.984 --> 15:46.351
just give him the money
from the backpack.

15:46.369 --> 15:47.852
Okay, okay. Don't shoot.

15:47.870 --> 15:49.472
Wha... It's empty.

15:49.506 --> 15:51.407
It's just Cheerios
and coloring books.

15:51.442 --> 15:53.076
What? Where the hell
is the money?

15:53.110 --> 15:54.744
Sir, we can't give you
any money,

15:54.778 --> 15:56.713
but if you've got
some milk and a bowl,

15:56.747 --> 15:59.148
we can give you a pretty
healthy way to start your day.

15:59.183 --> 16:00.350
All right,
enough of this.

16:00.384 --> 16:01.618
You, dog,

16:01.652 --> 16:03.519
pick which one of
you two is gonna die.

16:03.554 --> 16:06.290
What? You can't ask me
to decide something like that.

16:06.324 --> 16:09.627
The life of every being
is sacred, just like the life...

16:09.661 --> 16:10.961
Fine. I'll kill you.

16:10.996 --> 16:12.396
No, no, kill him.
He's a baby.

16:12.430 --> 16:13.897
He-he won't even remember
he was alive.

16:13.932 --> 16:15.099
You son of a b...

16:15.133 --> 16:17.468
(gunshot)
Aah! Stewie!

16:17.502 --> 16:20.387
Now, get us the
money you borrowed.

16:20.422 --> 16:22.657
Oh, my God, Stewie, no!

16:22.692 --> 16:24.693
(sobbing)

16:27.129 --> 16:29.064
Yeah, I was booked
for three hours

16:29.098 --> 16:31.232
by Archibald Meatpants.

16:31.267 --> 16:33.468
He's... he's dead.

16:33.502 --> 16:35.971
Okay, well, either way,
I'm getting paid,

16:36.005 --> 16:38.523
and somebody's
getting torn open.

16:42.229 --> 16:43.779
What the hell
are we gonna do, Stewie?

16:43.814 --> 16:45.514
We have no money,
no way to get home,

16:45.549 --> 16:47.583
and one of the loan shark's
goons is probably gonna bust

16:47.617 --> 16:49.485
through that door
any minute and kill us both.

16:49.519 --> 16:50.886
I wish my daddy were here.

16:50.921 --> 16:52.722
He always knows what to do.

16:53.724 --> 16:55.926
(engine starts)

16:55.960 --> 16:57.661
Oh, son of a bitch.

16:57.695 --> 16:59.029
Well, I better leave a note.

16:59.063 --> 17:00.597
It's the right thing to do.

17:04.736 --> 17:06.169
God, I've never felt
so hopeless.

17:06.204 --> 17:07.838
I mean, what are we
supposed to do?

17:07.872 --> 17:09.406
Just wait for them
to come kill us?

17:09.440 --> 17:10.774
Well, we could
go on the run.

17:10.808 --> 17:12.810
With what money?
And they'd still find us.

17:12.845 --> 17:14.365
Well, why don't we
just hitchhike home?

17:14.380 --> 17:15.663
Even if we could get
back there,

17:15.698 --> 17:17.965
we'd just be putting
the whole family in danger.

17:18.000 --> 17:19.967
(sighs) I don't see any way
out of this.

17:20.002 --> 17:22.704
Well, there is one
thing we could do.

17:22.738 --> 17:23.838
What? What's that?

17:23.872 --> 17:26.541
We could go out
on our own terms.

17:26.575 --> 17:28.076
What? You're saying
we should kill ourselves?

17:28.110 --> 17:29.178
Well, think about it.

17:29.212 --> 17:30.372
We're stuck here,
just waiting

17:30.380 --> 17:31.714
for some mobster
to do it.

17:31.748 --> 17:33.749
At least this way,
we can go out together.

17:33.783 --> 17:35.718
But think
about what you're saying.

17:35.752 --> 17:37.152
Brian, we're dead
no matter what.

17:37.187 --> 17:39.054
At least this way,
it'll be quick and clean.

17:39.089 --> 17:41.056
Well, not clean for the staff
of the hotel,

17:41.091 --> 17:43.125
but that's not really gonna be
our problem anymore.

17:43.159 --> 17:44.727
I-I don't know.

17:44.761 --> 17:46.796
Look, it's not like we've got
a lot to live for.

17:46.831 --> 17:48.331
I mean, I'm just gonna
end up like Chris,

17:48.366 --> 17:50.884
only I'll be smart enough
to realize how miserable I am.

17:50.918 --> 17:52.952
And you've only got
a few good years left anyway,

17:52.987 --> 17:55.121
and that's if we even get
out of here alive.

17:56.123 --> 17:57.857
(sighs)
All right, Stewie.

17:57.892 --> 18:00.093
Let's do it.

18:00.127 --> 18:01.694
Yeah, see, I'm glad
you came around.

18:01.729 --> 18:03.798
You know, the only thing
that was holding me back

18:03.832 --> 18:06.734
even a little is knowing how
much Lois is gonna milk this.

18:06.768 --> 18:10.304
Everyone, I truly want
to thank you for your support

18:10.338 --> 18:13.174
and remind you that,
as far as casseroles go,

18:13.208 --> 18:14.308
we're good on pasta,

18:14.342 --> 18:16.610
but we could use
some more dessert items.

18:16.645 --> 18:19.113
(sobbing)

18:19.147 --> 18:21.316
Oh, I miss my baby so much,

18:21.350 --> 18:22.984
and I'm more
of a chocolate person

18:23.019 --> 18:25.120
than a fruit person.

18:32.662 --> 18:34.529
Well, this is it.

18:34.564 --> 18:36.365
I guess so.

18:36.400 --> 18:38.034
Count to three?

18:38.068 --> 18:39.702
Yep.

18:39.736 --> 18:42.121
BOTH:
One, two...

18:42.156 --> 18:43.556
Three!
I'm sorry.

18:43.590 --> 18:44.907
I can't. I want to live!

18:44.942 --> 18:46.759
I didn't really think
we were gonna do it.

18:46.794 --> 18:49.095
You dick!

18:49.129 --> 18:50.530
Oh, my God, Brian!

18:50.564 --> 18:52.215
Brian, no!

18:52.249 --> 18:53.767
Good Lord, what have I done?

18:53.818 --> 18:55.719
I better get the hell
out of here.

18:55.753 --> 18:57.304
What the deuce?

18:57.338 --> 18:59.356
Where did this come from?

19:00.358 --> 19:02.726
Well, looks like
Archibald Meatpants

19:02.760 --> 19:04.661
is gonna have a fun night.

19:08.183 --> 19:09.868
One-way to Providence, please.

19:09.902 --> 19:12.187
Yeah, how much to get
to Providence?

19:12.221 --> 19:13.621
Brian?

19:13.656 --> 19:15.623
Stewie, what the hell?

19:15.658 --> 19:16.724
But how can you be...

19:16.759 --> 19:18.193
(gasps)
Oh, my God.

19:18.227 --> 19:20.228
C-Could it be?

19:20.262 --> 19:21.963
What the hell is going on?

19:21.997 --> 19:23.832
My teleportation machine worked.

19:23.866 --> 19:25.567
Of course it did;
that's how we got here.

19:25.634 --> 19:26.902
No, that's how
you got here.

19:26.937 --> 19:28.204
I flew.

19:28.238 --> 19:30.306
The machine must have
created two pairs of us--

19:30.340 --> 19:32.074
one that was teleported
to Las Vegas

19:32.108 --> 19:33.275
and the other that wasn't.

19:33.310 --> 19:34.944
You're kidding.
That's unbelievable.

19:34.978 --> 19:36.412
I know, it... Wait.

19:36.446 --> 19:37.813
Where's the other me?

19:37.848 --> 19:39.882
Oh, um... What?

19:39.916 --> 19:41.917
Where is the Stewie
you came with?

19:41.952 --> 19:45.322
Oh, well, th-these thugs
came to shoot you,

19:45.356 --> 19:48.024
and I tried to throw myself
in front of the bullet,

19:48.059 --> 19:50.727
but it must have gone, like,
under my armpit or something

19:50.761 --> 19:52.662
'cause it-it exploded
your face.

19:52.697 --> 19:54.264
Wait, what about
the other me?

19:54.298 --> 19:56.132
Oh, it was so sad.

19:56.167 --> 19:57.551
You took your own life.

19:57.585 --> 19:59.519
I tried like hell to
talk you out of it,

19:59.554 --> 20:01.055
but you jumped
off a balcony.

20:01.089 --> 20:02.790
People keep coming
back every hour

20:02.824 --> 20:04.242
because they think
it's a regular show,

20:04.276 --> 20:06.511
like-like the volcano or
the pirate ship thing.

20:06.545 --> 20:07.845
Wow.

20:07.880 --> 20:10.481
Well, I-I'm so glad
you're alive.

20:10.516 --> 20:11.899
Yeah, same with you.

20:11.934 --> 20:13.901
Well, we should
probably head home.

20:13.936 --> 20:15.102
Definitely.

20:15.137 --> 20:17.189
Um, uh, the only thing is,
I'm a little short.

20:17.223 --> 20:18.857
Is there any chance
you could cover me

20:18.892 --> 20:19.758
for the ticket?

20:19.792 --> 20:21.810
Oh, let me see
how much I have.

20:25.581 --> 20:28.016
Good news!
I have just enough.

20:28.051 --> 20:30.485
ANNOUNCER (over P.A.):
Now departing for Providence.

20:30.520 --> 20:32.087
<i>Hey, did you guys see O?</i>

20:32.121 --> 20:33.288
No, that seemed lame.

20:33.323 --> 20:35.341
You know, the other you
was a lot more fun.

20:35.376 --> 20:36.409
<i>Which one is O?</i>

20:36.443 --> 20:37.977
Is that the-the
swimming one?

20:38.012 --> 20:39.846
Don't-don't try to demean it.

20:39.880 --> 20:42.065
How does it feel to be
the least cultured person

20:42.099 --> 20:43.600
at a bus station?

20:57.566 --> 20:58.766
Hey.

20:58.800 --> 20:59.984
Hey.

20:59.985 --> 22:01.085
Thank you for watching «Family Guy» on
www.FOX-fan.ru